   "_dt": 1795429622.0,
   "ageDays": 1.38,
   "summary": "Unification Minister nominee Hong Ihk-pyo is a three-term lawmaker and a close political ally of President Lee Jae Myung with North Korea expertise. Before entering politics, he worked as a researcher at the Korea Institute for International Economic Policy and as a policy adviser to the Ministry of Unification. Hong served as floor leader of the ruling Democratic Party of Korea from September 2023 to May 2024 when Lee was party chair.",
   "summary_zh": "统一部长候选人洪仁烨是三届议员，也是总统李在明亲密的政治盟友，专长于朝鲜事务。进入政界前，他曾任韩国对外经济政策研究院研究员，并担任统一部政策顾问。2023年9月至2024年5月李在明担任党魁期间，洪仁烨出任朝鲜劳动党院内首席。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Unification Minister nominee Hong Ihk-pyo is a three-term lawmaker and a close political ally of President Lee Jae Myung with North Korea expertise. Born in 1967, he studied political science at Hanyang University. Before entering politics, he worked as a researcher at the Korea Institute for International Economic Policy and as a policy adviser to the Ministry of Unification. He also taught as a professor at the University of North Korean Studies. He won election to the National Assembly three times, serving from 2012 to 2024. Hong served as floor leader of the ruling Democratic Party of Korea from September 2023 to May 2024 when Lee was party chair. Earlier this year, Hong was appointed as senior presidential secretary for political affairs, handling coordination with the National Assembly and the political parties. If confirmed, he will succeed Chung Dong-young, who has served as unification minister since July last year",
